===BODY===
          <h2>Close to home</h2>
          <p>The Netherlands has direct ferry routes to England, including Hook of Holland to Harwich, Rotterdam to Hull and IJmuiden (near Amsterdam) to Newcastle, as well as a straightforward road route to the Channel through Belgium and France. That makes repatriation from Holland relatively quick and simple.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from anywhere in the Netherlands: Amsterdam, Rotterdam, The Hague, Utrecht, Eindhoven, Breda, and the ferry ports themselves. If your car broke down on the way to or from a ferry, we can pick it up near the terminal.</p>

          <h2>We speak Dutch</h2>
          <p>We can talk to the Dutch garage, storage company or recovery service directly in Dutch to arrange collection, so you don't need to. Just give us their name and phone number.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Missed your ferry because of a breakdown?</strong> Rebook your own crossing as a foot passenger or by car hire, and let us bring the car home separately.</p>
          </div>
===FAQ===
Q: Can you collect my car from a Dutch garage?
A: Yes. Send us the garage's name and address and we'll arrange it with them in Dutch. Make sure any fees there are settled.
Q: How long does it take?
A: From the Netherlands it's usually one of our quicker repatriations. We'll confirm the expected timing when we quote.
Q: Can you bring back a van?
A: Yes. We repatriate vans and light commercial vehicles too. Tell us the size and whether it's loaded.
